      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking some more, I\u0027m guessing that the parent thread doesn\u0027t change the state of mInputStream, mConnection after creating the background thread here?\n\nIf so, then I think that means that the _read_ access to mInputStream, mConnection from the unnamed background thread is safe (\"effectively immutable\", Java Concurrency in Practice chapter 3.5.4, page 53).\n\nAs far as I can tell, the _write_ access to mConnection, mInputStream, mCurrentOffset by the unnamed background thread is not synchronized or safely published back to the parent thread.\n\nDoes that make sense?",
